  "overview": "**AXA Slash Design System** is a light-first design system anchored on `#fff` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (19.7:1 contrast) and `#0275d8` brand accent.\n\nDisplay headlines pair `Georgia` with `Source Sans Pro` body copy (88px display down to 16px body), unified by `.25rem` base corner radius and subtle shadow elevation.\n\nMaintained by **AXA**. Source: published token package, package `@axa-fr/react-toolkit-all`. Inventory: **21** colors, **25** typography steps, and **56** documented components (MIT license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 56 component tokens with documented paddings: `.375rem .75rem`, `.8rem 1.2rem .8rem 1.2rem`, `.2rem .7rem`, `.5rem .75rem`, `.75rem 1rem`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `#f8f9fa` cards; separate sibling sections using `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Layered Shadow Model**: Uses documented shadows (`0 .25rem .75rem rgba(0,0,0,.1)`, `inset 0 -3px #00008f`) paired with `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` borders for elevated overlays.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#0275d8` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#fff` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `#0275d8` with `#f7f7f8` text (4.3:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `Georgia` headings with `Source Sans Pro` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `.25rem` base geometry across inputs and buttons (.25rem on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `#f8f9fa` surface shifts and `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `.25rem` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `input` fields and secondary buttons."
}
